# Introduction & Framework Overview {#introduction}

## Why This Framework Exists

Analytics projects fail for predictable reasons:
- Requirements are unclear or change mid-project
- Data quality issues discovered too late
- Stakeholders see the final product for the first time at delivery
- Analysis answers the wrong business question
- Projects take 2-3x longer than estimated

**This framework prevents these failures** through structured phases, clear checkpoints, and stakeholder alignment.

---

## Framework Philosophy

### Core Principles

**1. Front-Load the Thinking, Back-Load the Building**
Spend more time understanding the problem than solving it. Get clear on requirements before writing code.

**2. Show Work-in-Progress Early and Often**
Don't work in isolation. Weekly check-ins starting Week 1 prevent costly surprises.

**3. Build Trust Through Transparency**
Be honest about data limitations, timeline risks, and scope challenges. Stakeholders appreciate honesty.

**4. Perfect Is the Enemy of Done**
Deliver 80% of the value quickly, then iterate. Don't chase perfection while missing deadlines.

**5. Document for Your Future Self**
Write documentation as if you'll forget everything in 6 months. Because you will.

---

## The 5 Phases

```
DISCOVER          DEFINE            DEVELOP           DELIVER           DOCUMENT
(Week 1)          (Week 1-2)        (Week 2-4)        (Week 4-5)        (Week 5)
    │                 │                 │                 │                 │
    ├─ Context        ├─ Metrics        ├─ Build          ├─ Present        ├─ Lessons
    ├─ Kickoff        ├─ Mockup         ├─ Iterate        ├─ Feedback       ├─ Code docs
    ├─ Charter        ├─ Validate       ├─ Check-ins      ├─ Polish         ├─ Runbook
    └─ Research       └─ Sign-off       └─ Document       └─ Action items   └─ Transfer
```

**Timeline:** 4-5 weeks for typical project (adjust based on complexity)

---

## Success Factors

Your project is set up for success when:
- ✅ Business question is clear and documented
- ✅ Stakeholder sees work-in-progress weekly
- ✅ Data is validated before building complex logic
- ✅ Deliverable format is agreed upon upfront
- ✅ Scope and timeline are realistic and communicated

**If any of these are missing, your project is at risk.**

